.TH MYSTRCAT 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
mystrcat \- append one string to another
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "mystrfunctions.h"
.PP
.B int mystrcat(char *dest, const char *src);
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mystrcat
function appends the string pointed to by
.I src
to the end of the string pointed to by
.I dest.
The resulting string is terminated with a null character.
.PP
The destination buffer must have enough space for the original destination string,
the source string, and the terminating null character.
The function returns the length of the resulting string.
